From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] src/Makefile: link liblua.so with libm

Buildroot's 0002-shared-libs-for-lua.patch links liblua.so without
$(LIBS), so the library calls libm (sin, floor, ...) without a
DT_NEEDED entry for it. A program that loads liblua before libm, such
as rpm, then fails at startup:

  Relink `/lib64/liblua.so.5.4.8' with `/lib64/libm.so.6' for IFUNC symbol `sin'

Upstream: N/A, fixes Buildroot's own patch
Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Makefile b/src/Makefile
--- a/src/Makefile
+++ b/src/Makefile
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
 	$(RANLIB) $@
 
 $(LUA_SO): $(CORE_O) $(LIB_O)
-	$(CC) -o $@.$(PKG_VERSION) -shared -Wl,-soname="$@.$(PKG_VERSION)" $?
+	$(CC) -o $@.$(PKG_VERSION) -shared -Wl,-soname="$@.$(PKG_VERSION)" $? -lm
 	ln -fs $@.$(PKG_VERSION) $@
 
 ifneq (dynamic,$(BUILDMODE))
